#!/bin/sh
# launcher [drun|run]
# Primary: dmenu via Xwayland (same patched-dmenu options as the X11
# session). Fallbacks: tofi/bemenu. Uses the first available backend
# that supports the requested mode.
set -u

mode=${1:-drun}
case $mode in drun | run) ;; *)
  echo "launcher: mode must be drun or run" >&2
  exit 1
  ;;
esac

fail() {
  notify-send "launcher" "$1" 2>/dev/null || printf 'launcher: %s\n' "$1" >&2
  exit 1
}

if [ "$mode" = drun ]; then
  if command -v j4-dmenu-desktop >/dev/null && command -v dmenu >/dev/null; then
    exec j4-dmenu-desktop --dmenu='dmenu -c -l 10 -p "drun:" -i -bw 3 -F -h 35'
  elif command -v tofi-drun >/dev/null; then
    exec tofi-drun --drun-launch=true
  elif command -v j4-dmenu-desktop >/dev/null && command -v bemenu >/dev/null; then
    exec j4-dmenu-desktop --dmenu='bemenu -c -l 10 -p drun: -i'
  fi
  fail "no drun launcher found (dmenu+j4-dmenu-desktop/tofi/bemenu)"
else
  if command -v dmenu_run >/dev/null; then
    exec dmenu_run -c -l 10 -p "drun:" -i -bw 3 -F -h 35
  elif command -v bemenu-run >/dev/null; then
    exec bemenu-run -c -l 10 -p run: -i
  elif command -v tofi-run >/dev/null; then
    # tofi-run only prints the selection; launch it ourselves.
    sel=$(tofi-run) || exit 1
    [ -n "$sel" ] || exit 0
    exec setsid "$sel"
  fi
  fail "no run launcher found (dmenu/bemenu/tofi)"
fi
